3.) Shutdown Preparation Lead

Job Location: Port Harcourt, Rivers

Job Description


	The Shutdown Preparation Lead will support a major shutdown campaign on a FPSO. 
	He/she will be responsible for leading and coordinating all preparation activities required to ensure the safe and efficient execution of the offshore FFSD (Field Facility Shutdown).
	This role requires strong leadership capabilities, extensive shutdown/turnaround experience, and the ability to coordinate multidisciplinary teams in a complex offshore environment.


Responsibilities
The position we are offering involves the following main responsibilities :


	Lead and coordinate all preparation activities for the offshore FFSD campaign ;
	Manage and supervise a multidisciplinary team of preparators, including: Mechanical Static Equipment (Pressure Vessels, Piping, Valves), Structural discipline, Electrical & Instrumentation (E&I), Lifting operations, Materials and logistics coordination ;
	Compile, review, validate, and approve job packs and job cards ;
	Review and ensure the quality and completeness of technical documentation, including: Isometric drawings, Method Statements, Spading Plans, Isolation Plans, Lifting Plans, Job Risk Assessments (JRA)Conduct regular offshore site visits to monitor progress, resolve preparation issues, and ensure alignment between stakeholders ;
	Support shutdown planning activities, including work sequencing, resource allocation, and execution strategies ;
	Coordinate interfaces between engineering, operations, maintenance, contractors, and planning teams ;
	Ensure compliance with company HSE requirements and industry best practices throughout the preparation phase.


Required Profile


	You have at least 5 years of experience in the Oil & Gas process industry, with a proven experience in major shutdowns, turnarounds, or maintenance campaigns within offshore facilities, FPSOs, refineries, or petrochemical plants.
	You have a strong understanding of mechanical static equipment, piping systems, isolation processes, lifting operations, and E&I activities.
	You have demonstrated leadership and team coordination skills in a multicultural environment.
	You have excellent organizational, planning, and communication abilities.
	You are proficient in: Microsoft Excel, Microsoft Word, Microsoft PowerPoint.
	You are fluent in English (both written and spoken).


